.TH TINY 1 "2026-11-17" "TINY 2.1" "Games"
.SH NAME
tiny \- a quiz robot: a tiny neural network that answers questions, with a robot voice
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tiny
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tiny
is a neural network with 367,000 weights (4 layers, 96 wide) that reads and writes one letter at a time. It was written for DOS (Turbo C 2.0) and runs here
with the same network and a full-screen terminal interface: a chat window, a live neural monitor (the activity of every layer, the confidence in each letter, the speed),
a line for the question, and a robot voice that speaks the answer.
.PP
It was taught about 3,500 facts (all countries with their capitals, languages and neighbours, the chemical elements, animals, space, the body, simple sums and
times tables, opposites and plurals, some words in French, German, Spanish and Italian). On other questions it can answer confidently and be wrong.
.PP
The screen follows the size of the terminal (at least 60 x 14 characters). The neon colours want 256 colours; the launcher sets
.B TERM=xterm\-256color
when the terminal says plain xterm.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B 0 ... 9
creativity at the start: 0 always gives the surest answer (best for quizzes and sums), 5 is the default, 9 the freest.
.TP
.B /P
plain text mode, without the full-screen interface and the sound; it also starts when the input or the output is not a terminal, so
.B tiny < questions.txt
works.
.TP
.B /QUIET
start with the sound off.
.TP
.B /MONO
no colours.
.TP
.B /CLASSIC
the DOS colours instead of the neon palette.
.TP
.B /DEMO
the program asks a few questions itself.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Enter
ask the question.
.TP
.B PgUp, PgDn
the volume up and down, ten levels (the buttons in the toolbar of the terminal of the N900). The level is remembered in
.IR ~/.tiny\-volume .
.TP
.B Ctrl\-A
help (F1 in DOS).
.TP
.B Ctrl\-S
sound on or off (F2).
.TP
.B Ctrl\-V
robot voice on or off (F3).
.TP
.B Ctrl\-T
creativity 0 to 9 (F4).
.TP
.B Up arrow
the last question.
.TP
.B Esc
quit. In the line for the question the words
.B quit
and
.B exit
quit as well, and
.B cls
clears the screen.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TINY_BIN
the network file (default
.IR /opt/tiny/share/tiny/TINY.BIN ).
.TP
.B TINY_VOLUME
the volume, 1 to 10, for one run.
.TP
.B TINY_SILENT
if set, no sound.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/tiny/share/tiny/TINY.BIN
the trained network (380 kB).
.TP
.I ~/.tiny\-volume
the last volume.
.SH NOTES
The sound is played through
.BR paplay (1):
the sound policy of the N900 cuts the volume of a program it does not know to about 30 %, unless the stream sets its volume itself, as
.B paplay
does. So the volume of TINY is its own and does not follow the volume buttons of the phone.
.SH AUTHOR
TINY 2.1: https://github.com/WollyMonjac/Tiny\-2.1 ("written by Fable 5.2 and trained by Opus 5.5"). The port to the N900: https://github.com/n900\-resurrection/Tiny\-2.1.
